  "area": "discovery",
  "description": "AGSC-06-08 with AGSC-10-13: the boards link of the discovery document is present exactly when the node serves /boards/index.json — that is, when the Bundle holds a task — and absent otherwise; at Level 2 it carries type application/json and a digest. Two public Level-2 documents of one node with no peer, no successor, no declared surface and no contribution endpoint: with-a-board serves /boards/index.json and its document carries one rel#boards link with the SHA-256 of that file; without-a-board does not serve the route, and its document is the same document without that member — no other link and no bundle fact changes, because neither the counts nor graph.nq depend on the board export. Derivation, by hand: both documents are the public-level-2 document of disc-0020 with the rel#peer, rel#contribute and rel#surface members and the successor's alternate link removed (their inputs are absent here), and, for without-a-board, the rel#boards member removed. A conforming publisher given the input emits, after JCS (AGSC-04-04), exactly these bytes.",
